From ce3253c03ea13fb71d085bc69c1d3f2fcd58fe33 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: atomozero <bernardi.andrea@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 22:48:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 213/270] power: add tegra_dvfs, the supplies and clocks of the
 AC100

/dev/power/tegra_dvfs reports the core, CPU and RTC supplies of the
TPS6586x, the PLL, CPU and system bus clocks, and the speedo fuses
that tell which voltages this chip needs.

Writing "core <mV>", "cpu <mV>" or "rtc <mV>" moves a supply in
steps of 25 mV, within the limits of the AC100 device tree and keeping
the core 120 mV above the CPU and within 170 mV of the RTC domain, as
Linux does. U-Boot leaves the CPU at 1 GHz with 1.0 V, while the
Tegra 2 tables ask for 1.1 V at that rate.

Signed-off-by: atomozero <bernardi.andrea@gmail.com>
